      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parker%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s original post office opened in 1871 at Parker’s Landing, serving the Colorado River Indian Agency.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parker%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Arizona & California Railroad headquarters moved to Parker in 1991, replacing the Santa Fe Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parker%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Parker Historical Society preserves the community’s multicultural history and was once the Save The Jail Committee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://explore.localfirstaz.com/parker/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During World War II, Parker briefly housed over 17,000 Japanese Americans interned from the mainland.",
